{
  "_provenance": {
    "checkpoints": "best.ckpt and last.ckpt are PyTorch Lightning 2.5.5 checkpoints (best epoch 294, best val loss 1.140711e-02). The current code is plain PyTorch; testing/export.py reads that format, so the published model can be re-exported without retraining.",
    "edits_after_the_run": [
      "Removed eight keys the current code rejects as unimplemented: dataset.storage_dtype, dataset.skip_scan, dataset.skip_validate_grids, dataset.precompute_dt_table, dataset.uniform_offset_sampling_strict, dataset.assume_shared_grid, dataset.dt_epsilon, preprocessing.num_workers. They were live knobs in the paper-era code and are no-ops now.",
      "Removed the stale Lightning-era system.dtype, system.io_dtype and system.tf32; precision is owned by the precision block (the old system.tf32=true contradicted precision.tf32=false).",
      "Added training.warmup_start_factor=0.1, recovered from the SequentialLR state in best.ckpt (LinearLR start_factor 0.1, total_iters 10, then CosineAnnealingLR T_max 290, eta_min 5e-7). The key is required by src/trainer.py and was absent here.",
      "Added preprocessing.reuse_existing_data=true; the run reused existing shards (train.log line 9).",
      "paths.processed_data_dir: 'data' -> 'data/processed', which is what the run used (train.log line 9) and where normalization.json lives.",
      "paths.raw_data_files: [] -> the 382 files recorded in data/processed/normalization.json (meta.raw_data_files), the dataset this model was trained on."
    ],
    "record": "Hydrated config of the training run reported in Malsky et al., 'Accelerating Chemical Kinetics for Exoplanet Atmospheres using Neural Networks'. The run wrote it to models/big_flow; that directory is archived here as models/final_model. Model: residual encoder-operator-decoder, 11,577,356 trainable parameters.",
    "runnable_companion": "config/config_paper.jsonc restates this run in the current config schema, with comments. Train from that file, not this one.",
    "training_precision": "train.log lines 6 and 7 record 'TF32=True' and 'Lightning=bf16-mixed, Dataset=torch.bfloat16'. The precision block in this file is fp32 with tf32=false on purpose: the evaluation and export tooling (testing/export.py, accuracy.py, predictions.py, chemistry_estimates.py) loads this file on CPU or MPS, where src/utils.py hard-errors on anything but fp32. The paper's reported accuracy was evaluated in fp32. Use config/config_paper.jsonc to retrain at the run's precision."
  },
  "data": {
    "global_variables": [
      "P",
      "T"
    ],
    "species_variables": [
      "C2H2_evolution",
      "CH4_evolution",
      "CO2_evolution",
      "CO_evolution",
      "H2O_evolution",
      "H2_evolution",
      "HCN_evolution",
      "H_evolution",
      "N2_evolution",
      "NH3_evolution",
      "OH_evolution",
      "O_evolution"
    ],
    "time_variable": "t_time"
  },
  "dataset": {
    "batch_size_train": 2048,
    "multi_time_per_anchor": true,
    "num_workers": 4,
    "persistent_workers": true,
    "pin_memory": true,
    "prefetch_factor": 2,
    "preload_to_gpu": false,
    "times_per_anchor": 4,
    "use_first_anchor": true
  },
  "model": {
    "activation": "silu",
    "decoder_hidden": [
      1024,
      1024,
      1024,
      1024
    ],
    "dropout": 0.0,
    "dynamics_hidden": [
      1024,
      1024,
      1024,
      1024
    ],
    "dynamics_residual": true,
    "encoder_hidden": [
      1024,
      1024,
      1024,
      1024
    ],
    "latent_dim": 512,
    "mlp_only": false,
    "predict_delta": true,
    "predict_delta_log_phys": false,
    "softmax_head": false
  },
  "normalization": {
    "default_method": "log-standard",
    "epsilon": 1e-30,
